-- Q12791: Wealth Transfer and Gifting Strategies [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the net gift doctrine from Diedrich v. Commissioner, 457 U.S. 191 (1982), when donees agree to pay the gift tax, the taxable gift equals FMV minus the tax the donees will pay. This circular calculation reduces the effective tax cost compared to a traditional gift where the donor pays tax on the full value. The technique is supported by Treas. Reg. Section 25.2512-1.
Wrong (B): The IRS does not treat the donee''s payment as additional consideration increasing the taxable gift. The payment reduces the net transfer, lowering the tax base.
Wrong (C): Net gifts are not prohibited under Section 2512. The strategy is well-established and sanctioned by the Supreme Court in Diedrich.
Wrong (D): The donee''s tax payment is not treated as a separate taxable gift back to the donor. It reduces the taxable gift amount through the circular calculation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12791;

