-- Q13520: Owner-Entity Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 301 and the constructive dividend doctrine, when a corporation advances funds to a shareholder with no promissory note, no interest, no repayment schedule, and no actual repayments, the advance is recharacterized as a constructive dividend to the extent of E&P. The absence of genuine debt characteristics indicates no bona fide intent to repay.
