-- Q13580: Entity Formation and Restructuring [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRS Revenue Procedure 77-37, the ''substantially all'' assets requirement for a Type C reorganization under IRC Section 368(a)(1)(C) is met when the transferor conveys at least 70% of gross FMV and at least 90% of net FMV of all assets. Pine Corp''s transfer of 85% gross and 90% net exceeds both safe harbor thresholds.
Wrong (A): A 100% asset transfer is not required. The ''substantially all'' standard under Rev. Proc. 77-37 sets lower thresholds of 70% gross and 90% net FMV.
Wrong (C): There is no 95% threshold for Type C reorganizations. The IRS administrative safe harbor requires only 70% of gross assets and 90% of net assets.
Wrong (D): The built-in gain status of retained assets is irrelevant to the ''substantially all'' test. The standard is based solely on fair market value percentages.$EXPL$
